# The kata-flight lifecycle: the states Chris Wensel's shipping loop moves an item through,
# as a resource (`urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight`) rather than as a label namespace.
#
# In kata-flight these are `lifecycle:*` labels, "at most one" by convention, and a transition
# is a label remove followed by a label add — so a crash or a race between the two leaves an
# item with two of them, which its reaper then hunts for. Here the state is ONE value set by
# ONE store update (`urn:iki:ledger:{ledger}:item:{id}:state`), and this document is the
# vocabulary that update is checked against.
#
# The state names are kata-flight's. The DRAIN names are ours: each non-flight state names
# who picks an item up from it, which is the contract's rule that nothing parks outside the
# flight without saying who owns it. "No state" is the named state `filed`, declared here so
# that it has a drain too — absence is a state, not a residue.
#
# Every state's IRI is the lifecycle's IRI plus `:{name}`; the loader refuses anything else,
# because the state Sink writes the IRI it builds from a name.

@prefix ledger: <https://ikigai-rs.dev/ns/ledger#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:    <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight> a ledger:Lifecycle ;
    rdfs:label "kata-flight" ;
    rdfs:comment "kata-flight's shipping loop: select a wave, review-gate it, then per item claim it, resolve it in a worktree, refine it, ship it and close it." ;
    ledger:hasState
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:filed> ,
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:queued> ,
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:reviewed> ,
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:resolving> ,
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:refining> ,
        <urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:shipping> .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:filed> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "filed" ;
    rdfs:comment "Filed and in no wave yet. The item holds no ledger:state at all: absence is this state." ;
    ledger:order 0 ;
    ledger:inFlight false ;
    ledger:drain "triage" .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:queued> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "queued" ;
    rdfs:comment "Selected into a wave, waiting for the review gate." ;
    ledger:order 1 ;
    ledger:inFlight false ;
    ledger:drain "review-gate" .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:reviewed> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "reviewed" ;
    rdfs:comment "Passed the review gate; the ship loop claims it next." ;
    ledger:order 2 ;
    ledger:inFlight false ;
    ledger:drain "ship" .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:resolving> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "resolving" ;
    rdfs:comment "Claimed by the ship loop and being resolved in an isolated worktree." ;
    ledger:order 3 ;
    ledger:inFlight true .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:refining> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "refining" ;
    rdfs:comment "Resolved; being rebased and reviewed before it ships." ;
    ledger:order 4 ;
    ledger:inFlight true .

<urn:iki:ledger:lifecycle:kata-flight:shipping> a ledger:LifecycleState ;
    rdfs:label "shipping" ;
    rdfs:comment "Being fast-forward merged and closed." ;
    ledger:order 5 ;
    ledger:inFlight true .
